Z||000000||Hippocrat||11-02-2001||02:31 AM||||Has anybody figured out the magic code/sequence to unlock a Delco stereo after the power has been cut? <P>Seriously NASA doesn't guard their secrets as well as Delco does. This has got to be the best kept secret ever. Always figured that there was nothing you cant find on the net. Hell  you can find out how to make a nuke but not unlock these damned stereos LOL.<BR>(YES I do realize that this is the point)<P>Took it apart at one point on the off chance that there would be somewhere you could short it, kind of like you do on the PC mother boards. Not to say that there isn't but I did not find it.<BR>Thought about it afterward and got to thinking I didn't see a battery in there either so the code must be stored in the ROM itself. For lack of a better explanation (ever have to give yourself an explanation just to give you some piece of mind? and allow your self to get back to your life)<P>Anyway I sucked it up, admitted defeat, took it to the dealer and paid my 30 bucks. <P>Its out of a 95 cav.<P>I believe that it is just a default override code that allows them to reset the security code. Its not the cost that bothers me, its the not knowing.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by Hippocrat (edited 11-02-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Hippocrat (edited 11-02-2001).]||||reg||1
